Third-party material redistributed in this repository
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository packages third-party cloud-native applications as OCM (Open
Component Model) components. Most of that packaging is metadata that references
upstream artifacts rather than copying them. The following files, however, are
copies of upstream material and remain subject to their upstream licenses:

  keycloak/operator/operator.yml
  keycloak/operator/keycloaks-crd.yml
  keycloak/operator/keycloakrealmimports-crd.yml

    Keycloak Operator installation manifests and CustomResourceDefinitions,
    version 26.4.5, taken verbatim from the Keycloak project.

    Keycloak — https://github.com/keycloak/keycloak
    Copyright the Keycloak Authors
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Upstream projects referenced by these components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The component descriptors in this repository reference container images and Helm
charts published by the projects below. Those artifacts are not stored in this
repository; they are resolved from their upstream registries at build or transfer
time and remain under their own licenses.

  Alpine Linux         https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine          MIT (see below)
  Argo Workflows       https://github.com/argoproj/argo-workflows      Apache-2.0
  cert-manager         https://github.com/cert-manager/cert-manager    Apache-2.0
  CloudNativePG        https://github.com/cloudnative-pg/cloudnative-pg  Apache-2.0
  etcd                 https://github.com/etcd-io/etcd                 Apache-2.0
  Flux                 https://github.com/fluxcd/flux2                 Apache-2.0
  Keycloak             https://github.com/keycloak/keycloak            Apache-2.0
  nginx (LinuxServer)  https://github.com/linuxserver/docker-nginx     GPL-3.0 (see below)
  PostgreSQL           https://github.com/cloudnative-pg/postgres-containers  PostgreSQL License
  Zot                  https://github.com/project-zot/zot              Apache-2.0

Two of those need a word of explanation:

  - The Alpine base image aggregates packages from the Alpine repositories, each
    under its own license. MIT covers Alpine's own material, not the contents of
    the image as a whole.
  - GPL-3.0 is the license of LinuxServer.io's image build for nginx. nginx
    itself is BSD-2-Clause; the image bundles both.

Note that transferring a component by value (for example
`ocm transfer --copy-resources`) copies those upstream artifacts into the target
registry or transport archive. Redistribution of the resulting archive is subject
to the licenses of the artifacts it carries.
